==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Jizo's Moving Castle''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Jizo's Mega-Castle''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Ultra Kasa Jizo''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stone]]s and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Kasa Jizo has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Kasa Jizo is cheap with a very short cooldown, so a stack of them will annihilate most [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies in their path. Once leveled up, Kasa Jizo is extremely powerful on Dark-dominant stages like [[Gestalt, Decay]], [[Soap Scum]] and the [[:Category:XP Guerrilla Stages|XP Stages]] (though [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] is nearly essential for [[Taste of Success (Merciless)|Merciless XP!]]), as well as Angel-heavy stages like [[Broken Mask]] and [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]]. Even against other enemies, he still has fine stackable DPS, about 50% more than that of a [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] of equal level at the cost of some range.

Thanks to the combination of range and short cooldown, Kasa Jizo is also usable as a pseudo-meatshield in certain stages where the use of short ranged cats is ill-advised, notably against wave enemies or certain Long Distance ones, such as in [[Darkweb]] against [[Dober P.D]] where [[Gory Dark]] may occasionally harass your frontlines.

Kasa Jizo works well as a stackable midranger generalist assuming you don't have other units that can replace him, thanks to his short cooldown, good stats and spammability, though later on he may get outclassed by other units due to generalist value being less sought after due to how mixed stages can get, not to mention other units like [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] being able to take on [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] with Behemoth Slayer, Wave Immunity and usage in 4-Crown Legend Stages and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] having more bulk to last longer in battle. However, Kasa Jizo has the edge of better cooldown, range and stackability.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Jizo's Moving Castle can be very useful on stages with powerful, decently-ranged bosses with supporting Dark or Angel enemies, such as the [[Absolute Defense (Insane)|Crazed Tank]] and [[Vulcanizer (Deadly)|Manic Eraser]] stages. In some cases, the boss might also be a Dark or Angel enemy like [[Angry Fighting]] or [[Spa of Ascension]]. His range of 450 is good enough to outrange most enemies, further improved by the massive damage ability, which is very helpful as some mid-late game threats are Dark or Angel. A level 50 Moving Castle has a whopping 150k HP and a grand 129,600 damage. That's up to 518,400 against Dark and Angels, enough to kill almost anything in only a few hits! Even better, the generalist usage for the moving castle is quite good.

With all this being said, the moving castle has two flaws that drag it down: its knockbacks and attack rate. Both are lacking and, should an enemy creep in during its attack cooldown, the moving castle may be as good as dead. Luckily, the castle's problems are lessened in its True Form.

Jizo's Moving Castle should still be used in place of the normal form in some cases, as some enemies outrange it and cannot be easily countered. [[Winged Pigge]], [[St. Dober]] and [[Othom]] are the most prominent enemies countered by this improvement, while less notable enemies this also helps against include [[Master A.]], [[Project A]], [[THE SLOTH]] and [[Le'noir]].

==='''True Form'''===
Kasa Jizo's main use lies in his Normal Form for stackability, a very important point for those who have proceeded far into the game. This, unfortunately, means that there is very little point in acquiring his True Form outside of acquiring his Ultra Form; but if you do, it is not a bad idea, as Jizo's Mega-Castle has its attack cooldown shortened, gains more health and more range, at the cost of a multi-hit attack. The problem with multi-hit is that it may cause Jizo's Mega-Castle to miss against enemies with many knockbacks, shown prominently when used against Winged Pigge in [[Heaven's Oasis]]. However, it also has its benefits, as it can knock back powerful but fast enemies, especially [[Angelic Gory]], back so that the last hit may land more easily.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Ultra Kasa Jizo reverts the unit to its Normal Form but with additional stat boosts and abilities. There are two main reasons to get this Ultra Form: one, for the [[Survive|Survive]] ability that provides Jizo with incredible staying power, together with the HP boost that work in tandem to make it nigh-impossible for enemies to put him down for good; and two, to give Jizo's Normal Form access to powerful Talents, including stat boosts that drastically improve his generalist usage by raising his HP/DPS up to 42,240 and ~4,702 respectively, completely outperforming the likes of a max-investment Lv.50+80 Cyborg Cat in everything but range. The magnitude of this boost becomes even more apparent against specialist options like Mushroom Cat and [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], where the sheer stat differences, combined with his utility and spammability, now blow them out of the water against their respective target traits.

You can also fully utilize [[Talent Orbs]] to enhance his [[Massive Damage|Massive Damage]] ability against either Angel or Dark enemies, but with how difficult they are to obtain, this is just a small bonus for endgame players. Additionally, [[Omni Strike]] doesn't do much to help Jizo outside of giving the player a small amount of leeway should peons intersect more pressing threats.

Outside of the aforementioned differences, everything in Jizo's Normal Form description applies here but to greater effect. He effectively becomes a conglomerate mix of the best aspects of many spammable units, creating a powerful supersoldier. Despite how simple of an investment this is, especially for [[Catseye|Dark Catseyes]], it isn't a bad one by any stretch of the imagination. Even when pitted up against the likes of [[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-10 Gigapult]] and [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Windy α]], this Ultra Form remains a top priority in spite of its extreme cost.

==='''Talents'''===
Jizo's Mega-Castle can gain an immunity to Curse and Toxic, both of which can have their uses. The main draw of '''[[Immune to Curse]]''' is to continue the hard hits even in the face of Relic enemies and the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]. This may be situational when dealing with Angel and Dark enemies, but it can certainly come in handy.
*In Ultra Form, this ability is primarily useful in mixed [[Uncanny Legends]] stages that feature oppressive melee/midranged Relic spam, like [[Sir Rel]]s and [[M. Ost]], alongside Dark/Angels to ensure he retains the Massive Damage ability even in his final reposition. It can also find some use in infiltrating [[Loris]]' blind spot, or as an extra level of security against enemies that otherwise outrange him like [[Othom]] should your units push too far into enemy backlines.

'''[[Immune to Toxic|Toxic Immunity]]''' is also situational due to the relatively low numbers of enemies with Toxic attacks. This talent can certainly help against [[Casaurian Darkjo]], [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]], and the peons supporting [[Big Peng Z]], so this Talent is worth considering for players who struggle with these enemies.
*The same applies in Ultra Form, although it can also counter [[Zollow]]s and [[Gobble]]s very well, similarly to a Talented Cyborg Cat (but better).

'''Resist Surge''' is next. Surges do appear alongside Darks and Angels, albeit rarely. Unfortunately, while the Mega-Castle's high HP and range are good, Surges can still do a number even when resisted. It can certainly tank a few, but surge spam stages still wreck this castle.
*Ultra Kasa Jizo's lower HP when compared to Jizo's Mega-Castle leads to a far less forgiving threshold of damage that can put him into Survive range, regardless of whether this Talent is unlocked. It is better to invest into Defense Buff before even considering this Talent. Even with this, it can still see good practical application against [[St. Dober]], or in Aku centric stages that feature Death Surges.

Finally, Jizo's Mega-Castle gets the standard '''Attack Buff''' and '''Defense Buff''' Talents. As a nuker (or DPS in Ultra Form), Attack Buff is usually preferred, as the high range does a good enough job keeping Jizo safe from damage.

==='''Orb'''===
When it comes to Effect Orbs, Massive Damage Up against Dark or Angel is the ideal choice for either of the forms it's available to.

As for Ability Orbs, Berserker Orb can see usage given the role of Jizo's Mega-Castle as a backline nuker (with multi-hit giving the Mega-Castle an opportunity to activate it for subsequent hits), meanwhile Surge Resist Orb can be combined with a maxed out Surge Resist Talent to provide effective [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]].
*For Ultra Kasa Jizo, Cash Back or Cost Reduction Orbs can be used to alleviate the cash drain from the fast recharge, although Cost Reduction is generally preferred as the former's caveat of requiring the unit to die is counterintuitive to maximizing his value. The aforementioned Surge Resist Orb + Surge Resist Talent combination is also a good choice for stages with St. Dober or Aku enemies. As a generalist unit, Ultra Kasa Jizo could also benefit from Dodge Orb, thanks to his Survive ability, but is generally less worthwhile than alternatives.

