==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Kasa Jizo was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Ancient Heroes (Removed Combo)|Ancient Heroes]] and [[Ultra Souls (Removed Combo)|Ultra Souls]].
*Kasa Jizo has the shortest recharge time of all [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]].
*Jizo's Moving Castle is mentioned in one of [[Gamatoto Expedition|Gamatoto's logs]], "... in Jizo's Moving Castle."
*This unit is based on [[wikipedia:Kasa Jizō|Kasa Jizō]], a tale about an old man who offered some kasas, which are feudal-era Japanese hats, to six Jizo Statues covered in snow when he was unable to sell any of them. Since he only had five hats, he offered his own to the last statue. (which explains the hat-less Jizo in this cat's evolved form). The statues subsequently repay him for his virtuous deed. In the gallery above, there are examples of kasa hats and a Jizō statue.
*Jizo's Moving Castle is based on the film adaptation of [[wikipedia:Howl's Moving Castle (film)|Howl's Moving Castle]], especially on the legs.
*Jizo's Moving Castle is called Kamui in The Battle Cats POP!
*Kasa Jizo's weapon is similar to a [[wikipedia:Revolver|Revolver]], and Ultra Kasa Jizo's weapon is similar to a [[wikipedia:Heckler & Koch MP5#MP5K|MP5K]]. Although both fire multiple times, they only land one hit at 19f.

